recurSaveT -- SEQ 373 (Tony, 2026-10-16): recursion's save/restore on the INTERPRETED road, measure only. Its twin is
incant/pop/jit/jitRecurSaveT, its own process. RS-1: t = n; r = f(n-1); r = r + t -- t must survive the recursive call
(per-activation locals), f(4) = 4+3+2+1 = 10. RS-2: r = g(n-1); r = r + n -- the ARGUMENT read after the call returns,
g(4) = 10. R1: the cap writes nothing -- `if argument < 0; return -1;` stops a downward overshoot with a named wrong value, and
pop.sh's POPCAP fails any other runaway BY NAME as a timeout. A depth COUNTER was tried first and perturbed the very thing
measured: its `+=` reuses the shared scratch node a computed argument (`argument - 1`) is bound to, so every callee read
its argument as the counter's value (measured 2026-10-16: 4, 2, 3, 4, 5 ... on the way down).
